WEBVTT

00:04.462 --> 00:06.089
[intriguing music playing]

00:14.222 --> 00:16.141
[deep ragged breathing]

00:22.522 --> 00:24.733
Where did you disappear to?

00:25.900 --> 00:29.654
No one could ever take your place.

00:30.447 --> 00:35.035
Everyone here... tried to become you.

00:35.118 --> 00:36.453
[snarling]

00:38.079 --> 00:41.124
But just as I thought no one could...

00:41.207 --> 00:42.876
[tense music building]

00:44.961 --> 00:46.379
PAPER PLANE
WITH FOLDING GUIDE

00:46.463 --> 00:47.672
[door squeaking open]

00:50.467 --> 00:52.427
[door closes, creaking]

00:52.510 --> 00:54.179
[deep ragged breathing]

01:03.688 --> 01:06.775
Please come back soon.

01:06.858 --> 01:08.234
[music fades]

01:13.740 --> 01:15.617
Aw, man.

01:15.700 --> 01:18.119
I can't seem to find them anywhere!

01:19.037 --> 01:21.581
But at least my information was reliable.

01:22.082 --> 01:25.752
The Cross-Eyes' hideout must be
somewhere here in Berith.

01:26.252 --> 01:30.173
LET'S USE OUR RESOURCES WITH CARE
BERITH NEWS

01:32.926 --> 01:36.763
Let's see,
how many years has it been since I died?

01:39.808 --> 01:41.184
[vendor] Found everything?

01:44.646 --> 01:46.106
[man] My apologies,

01:46.189 --> 01:48.942
I was planning to pay
with coupon points today,

01:49.025 --> 01:51.152
so I didn't bring my wallet...

01:51.653 --> 01:53.863
Ugh, are you serious?

01:53.947 --> 01:56.616
Fine... I'll let it slide, just this once.

01:56.699 --> 01:57.700
Thank you.

01:58.743 --> 01:59.577
Huh?

02:01.329 --> 02:02.413
Huh?

02:03.039 --> 02:04.374
Okay. I'll... I'll be back.

02:04.457 --> 02:05.542
[vendor] Whatever.

02:06.417 --> 02:07.836
Welcome, sir.

02:08.419 --> 02:10.088
That's 130 nicks.

02:11.673 --> 02:12.966
Come again!

02:13.049 --> 02:14.592
BALLMART

02:15.260 --> 02:16.594
- [man] Yo!
- [Risu] Hm?

02:19.222 --> 02:20.682
Got a problem?

02:20.765 --> 02:22.976
[man] You're Risu, aren't you?

02:24.435 --> 02:25.311
[gasps]

02:25.395 --> 02:27.522
[man] Though I'm sure you don't know me...

02:29.524 --> 02:31.609
[frantic electronic music playing]

02:43.913 --> 02:45.540
[lyrics in Japanese]

03:56.819 --> 03:57.862
[music fades]

03:57.946 --> 03:58.947
THE BEGINNING

04:08.790 --> 04:10.708
This here is our hideout.

04:10.792 --> 04:12.210
[intriguing music playing]

04:13.628 --> 04:14.629
Uh...

04:15.338 --> 04:16.172
[gasps]

04:17.382 --> 04:21.552
I... I didn't think
it would be such a normal house!

04:21.636 --> 04:25.556
I imagined something
with more secret society vibes...

04:27.392 --> 04:29.811
- Huh?
- [man] I bought some rice.

04:32.063 --> 04:33.314
Hey, guys.

04:33.398 --> 04:34.941
Risu is here.

04:36.234 --> 04:37.318
[Risu] Uh...

04:45.243 --> 04:46.452
Uh...

04:47.954 --> 04:50.164
Isn't it a bit too dark in here?

04:50.665 --> 04:52.667
Why don't you turn on the lights?

04:53.710 --> 04:56.587
We have a rule. No lights in the daytime.

04:57.213 --> 04:59.090
Hey, pour him some tea.

04:59.173 --> 05:02.468
[man 2] It's a good thing
I saved yesterday's tea bag.

05:02.552 --> 05:04.012
[man 3] Here you go.

05:04.554 --> 05:06.014
Uh... ugh.

05:06.097 --> 05:08.558
[man] I heard somewhere
that you were dead.

05:08.641 --> 05:11.728
[sighs] Yeah, and now I'm looking for
the guy who killed me!

05:11.811 --> 05:15.982
[man 3] The guy who killed you?
What do you mean? You're alive.

05:16.065 --> 05:17.734
[seethes] I was brought back!

05:17.817 --> 05:19.986
Through the Magic of En's pet!

05:20.069 --> 05:22.238
- Yeah, by Karaage.
- [man] Kikurage.

05:25.325 --> 05:28.745
The one who killed me
was a Cross-Eyes Man.

05:29.245 --> 05:30.747
I witnessed it myself!

05:30.830 --> 05:34.000
Where is he?
Where's the boss? Let me see him now!

05:34.083 --> 05:35.043
Otherwise...

05:36.794 --> 05:39.130
[man] Why don't we all relax?

05:41.424 --> 05:45.053
We know as much as you do.
We've no idea how or why you died.

05:45.136 --> 05:46.262
[grunts]

05:46.346 --> 05:47.930
[man 4] Old newspapers! Old magazines!

05:48.014 --> 05:50.058
- Wait! Do you guys hear that?
- [gasps]

05:50.141 --> 05:51.642
[man 4] Feel free to call out to me

05:51.726 --> 05:53.603
if there's anything
you don't need anymore.

05:53.686 --> 05:55.813
Old newspapers! Old magazines!

05:56.481 --> 05:57.940
It's the old newspaper collector!

05:58.024 --> 06:01.652
We can swap five stacks of old newspapers
for three rolls of toilet paper!

06:02.153 --> 06:03.321
Go after the collector!

06:04.697 --> 06:07.367
[collector] Old newspapers, old magazines.

06:08.117 --> 06:10.661
Hoo, that was a surprise.

06:10.745 --> 06:13.206
That collector is so hard to track down.

06:13.289 --> 06:17.460
Who cares about old newspapers?
Someone turn on the lights already!

06:17.543 --> 06:20.463
No. We won't until the sun has set.

06:20.546 --> 06:22.131
[uneasy music playing]

06:24.675 --> 06:26.010
[Risu grumbles]

06:26.094 --> 06:28.721
Give me a break here, you guys.

06:29.597 --> 06:33.726
I think it's gotten plenty dark outside
by now, don't you?

06:34.769 --> 06:37.146
[man] Well, it is starting
to affect our work.

06:37.647 --> 06:39.732
- I think it's about time.
- [man 2] Right.

06:40.441 --> 06:41.359
[grunts]

06:42.026 --> 06:43.694
[intriguing music playing]

06:44.946 --> 06:46.864
I'm Tetsujo. Good to meet ya.

06:46.948 --> 06:47.990
I'm Ton.

06:48.074 --> 06:48.991
Saji.

06:49.075 --> 06:50.493
I'm Ushishimada.

06:51.077 --> 06:52.578
My name is Dokuga.

06:53.079 --> 06:56.541
Yeah, I know those names.
I've heard them before.

06:56.624 --> 06:58.751
You're the guys closest to the boss!

06:58.835 --> 07:02.255
More importantly,
how long do you plan to stay here?

07:02.338 --> 07:03.423
[scoffs]

07:03.506 --> 07:07.009
Sounds like my sticking around here
might bring you some trouble, huh?

07:07.093 --> 07:10.346
What I mean is
we don't have food to feed you dinner.

07:10.430 --> 07:11.264
You got that?

07:11.347 --> 07:12.974
Come on, boys! Time to eat!

07:13.057 --> 07:15.184
[Ton] Who was in charge of cooking today?

07:17.728 --> 07:19.397
[man] The boss is this way.

07:21.607 --> 07:23.693
Welcome. Come in!

07:23.776 --> 07:25.445
What are you doing, Ebisu?

07:25.945 --> 07:28.573
[Ebisu] Didn't you hear?
They're putting me to work.

07:29.073 --> 07:32.201
They say that those who do no work,
shall not eat, don't they?

07:32.285 --> 07:35.496
[Ebisu] I'm the seductive
man-eating mermaid,

07:35.580 --> 07:37.206
Erabisu. [chuckles]

07:37.290 --> 07:41.002
[Noi] "Man-eating," huh?
Is this a cannibal club?

07:41.085 --> 07:42.962
[Ebisu] It's a figure of speech.

07:43.045 --> 07:45.965
- Good, you're here.
- [squawks]

07:46.048 --> 07:47.383
[En] You, alchohol.

07:47.467 --> 07:48.968
Yes, Big Boss!

07:49.051 --> 07:51.721
- You, bring them some women.
- [man 2] Yes!

07:51.804 --> 07:53.306
[Noi] Who needs women?

07:55.808 --> 07:58.102
- Good evening.
- Oh... [chuckles] Hi.

07:58.186 --> 08:00.146
Hey big fella.

08:00.646 --> 08:01.772
[gasps]

08:01.856 --> 08:03.816
[Fujita] Oh, it's you two! Hey!

08:03.900 --> 08:05.318
[chuckling]

08:05.401 --> 08:07.778
You even got Fujita working here too?

08:07.862 --> 08:11.574
I volunteered to take care
of Mr. En's daily needs!

08:11.657 --> 08:15.077
He follows me everywhere now.
He's annoying as hell, to be honest.

08:15.161 --> 08:16.829
[Fujita chuckling]

08:17.663 --> 08:21.584
[Fujita] Nikaido, don't you think
you're fooling anyone.

08:21.667 --> 08:24.587
I'll keep Mr. En safe from you
no matter what!

08:24.670 --> 08:26.088
Like I said.

08:26.172 --> 08:28.007
[Ebisu panting]

08:29.675 --> 08:31.052
Here are...

08:31.135 --> 08:31.969
[pants]

08:32.053 --> 08:33.304
...your Martinis.

08:33.387 --> 08:35.598
- [panting]
- [En] There's been some news.

08:36.182 --> 08:37.600
I finally found it.

08:38.100 --> 08:40.853
The place that has been making
the Black Powder.

08:40.937 --> 08:42.355
- [Shin] Huh?
- For real?

08:42.438 --> 08:44.106
[En] It's just a rumor,

08:44.190 --> 08:46.859
but I hear there's a hideout
in some forest somewhere.

08:46.943 --> 08:48.653
Some forest somewhere?

08:48.736 --> 08:51.614
If that's all you got,
you haven't found it at all, idiot!

08:53.074 --> 08:55.493
- Then you must think he's there too?
- [Noi gasps]

08:55.576 --> 08:58.996
Maybe so. At least, that's what I suspect.

08:59.080 --> 09:01.874
Oh my God.
You mean the leader of the Cross-Eyes?

09:01.958 --> 09:03.376
I saw it in the movie!

09:03.459 --> 09:06.170
Oh, babe,
you were so wonderful in that! Seriously!

09:06.254 --> 09:07.255
[En chuckles]

09:07.338 --> 09:08.589
I was, wasn't I?

09:08.673 --> 09:11.842
[gasps] The scene where the family
gets created. I have chills...

09:11.926 --> 09:15.680
Is it just me, or does Nikaido seem
to be acting more like Chota?

09:15.763 --> 09:17.765
Yeah, I think so too.

09:17.848 --> 09:21.227
The poor girl's got
her entire personality twisted up.

09:21.727 --> 09:23.729
[puffing]

09:25.231 --> 09:29.026
I do feel bad for Nikaido,
but at least we all get to live!

09:29.110 --> 09:30.403
Ha, what a relief.

09:30.486 --> 09:34.240
You said it.
It was time I gave up on her anyway.

09:34.865 --> 09:37.410
She's a sorcerer.
We were never meant to be.

09:37.493 --> 09:41.330
I think a sorcerer and a human
can get along no problem.

09:43.374 --> 09:48.004
Still, it would be great to fill Caiman in
about the current situation, at least.

09:48.087 --> 09:49.297
[crazed grunting]

09:50.047 --> 09:51.299
[coughing]

09:51.382 --> 09:52.800
[sighs contentedly]

09:53.384 --> 09:54.677
[sighs contentedly]

09:55.386 --> 09:57.263
[crazed grunting]

09:58.389 --> 09:59.765
Huh. You know what?

09:59.849 --> 10:03.811
Seen as Caiman is totally immune to Magic,
he might be able to save Nikaido.

10:04.395 --> 10:08.232
I agree, but we don't know
where Caiman is right now.

10:09.108 --> 10:10.818
[Kasukabe] Let's send him a messenger.

10:13.654 --> 10:15.823
But... who'd go?

10:17.283 --> 10:18.868
I was thinking my wife.

10:20.411 --> 10:22.830
Thank you for your patronage!

10:22.913 --> 10:25.333
We hope to see you again soon!

10:25.416 --> 10:27.001
[intriguing music playing]

10:27.793 --> 10:31.380
He's definitely still alive.
Don't you think so, Noi?

10:31.464 --> 10:32.965
Yeah, I do.

10:33.049 --> 10:35.343
If we only knew his face,

10:35.426 --> 10:38.387
there would be so many ways
to be able to find him.

10:39.138 --> 10:42.266
His face was so drenched
in Tenjin's blood,

10:42.350 --> 10:46.604
I couldn't even see the crosses
that were supposed to be on his eyes.

10:48.022 --> 10:53.903
En's movie has a lot of crap,
but it's true that guy almost killed us.

10:58.699 --> 11:00.284
[Noi grunting excitedly]

11:01.410 --> 11:03.621
Things are finally
getting interesting again.

11:03.704 --> 11:06.290
And I swear that this time I won't lose!

11:06.374 --> 11:07.625
[Shin chuckling]

11:08.209 --> 11:10.920
- That's what I like about you, Noi.
- Huh?

11:11.504 --> 11:15.174
No matter how dangerous the job,
you're never gonna slow me down.

11:15.257 --> 11:16.175
[chuckling]

11:16.676 --> 11:18.260
Back at ya, Shin.

11:21.013 --> 11:25.851
We left without a word to Shin.
He's probably furious right about now.

11:25.935 --> 11:28.938
Well, I did leave a note,
so it should be fine.

11:29.021 --> 11:31.148
I'm sorry it's so cramped, Johnson.

11:31.232 --> 11:32.441
[grunts] Shocking!

11:32.525 --> 11:34.318
[crazed grunting]

11:34.402 --> 11:35.695
- [Shin] Hmm?
- [Noi] Huh?

11:37.071 --> 11:38.447
Will they be okay?

11:38.531 --> 11:41.826
If someone finds out they're humans,
they'll wind up on an auction block.

11:41.909 --> 11:44.829
They said they'll come back by morning.
Let them be.

11:45.496 --> 11:47.123
- Oh!
- [Noi grunts]

11:50.000 --> 11:51.293
Thank you.

11:51.377 --> 11:54.213
Look, Shin,
why don't I go out and bring 'em back?

11:54.296 --> 11:56.632
Relax! Why would you need to do that?

11:56.716 --> 12:00.219
[Noi] Eh, I've been bored lately,
I have all this spare energy.

12:00.302 --> 12:01.846
- [door opens]
- Hey, Noi, wait--

12:01.929 --> 12:03.848
Too late. I'm off!

12:04.473 --> 12:05.516
- Hey!
- [door closes]

12:07.101 --> 12:09.103
[sighs] What can you do?

12:12.064 --> 12:15.443
[Thirteen] Hey, Professor, so how long's
it been since you last saw your wife?

12:15.526 --> 12:19.363
- [Kasukabe] Hmm. About 25 years, maybe?
- [Thirteen] Huh?

12:19.447 --> 12:21.532
Are you sure she just didn't dump you?

12:21.615 --> 12:24.618
Based on her age,
there's a chance she's dead already.

12:24.702 --> 12:26.370
- Oh, come on!
- Huh?

12:27.163 --> 12:28.497
There's a house.

12:30.624 --> 12:33.461
[crazed growling]

12:33.544 --> 12:35.421
Huh? What's wrong, Johnson?

12:35.504 --> 12:37.631
Ha! He got stuck and can't get out.

12:37.715 --> 12:38.883
[growling]

12:38.966 --> 12:41.886
Just wait here for a second.
We'll be right back.

12:41.969 --> 12:43.220
[ominous music stab]

12:44.472 --> 12:46.766
[whimpers] I'm scared.

12:46.849 --> 12:49.018
- [eerie music playing]
- [knocking on door]

12:49.852 --> 12:51.687
[Kasukabe] Maybe she's not home?

12:51.771 --> 12:54.273
- Oh, it's open.
- [Thirteen] Wait, hang on!

12:54.356 --> 12:55.274
[door squeaking]

13:00.488 --> 13:03.407
HORROR! BLOODY MANSION SLAUGHTER DANCE.

13:03.491 --> 13:06.035
- [whimpering]
- There's no way this is the right place!

13:06.118 --> 13:07.870
We can't say that for sure.

13:07.953 --> 13:10.414
The professor's house looks
quite similar to this.

13:10.498 --> 13:11.415
What the hell?!

13:13.000 --> 13:14.168
Huh?

13:14.794 --> 13:16.128
This is weird.

13:16.212 --> 13:18.422
Everything in here, it's almost as if...

13:19.048 --> 13:22.676
Looks like there's another room
in the back. Huh?

13:25.554 --> 13:26.514
[gasps]

13:27.973 --> 13:30.226
- What the...?!
- [pained groaning]

13:32.144 --> 13:33.813
[deep ragged breathing]

13:35.147 --> 13:37.066
[ragged breathing]

13:38.651 --> 13:40.361
[clown laughing creepily]

13:40.444 --> 13:43.072
What's the matter, ladies? Are you lost?

13:43.155 --> 13:44.448
[shrieking laughter]

13:46.075 --> 13:47.159
They're not.

13:47.243 --> 13:50.454
This is the worthy prey
that he has set down in front of us.

13:51.247 --> 13:52.957
[whimpering fearfully]

13:53.040 --> 13:53.958
[gasps]

13:54.041 --> 13:55.960
I think we might have the wrong house.

13:56.043 --> 13:57.211
Johnson! Come here!

13:57.294 --> 13:58.879
[warbling]

13:59.797 --> 14:00.923
[both grunting]

14:01.006 --> 14:02.258
[all grunting]

14:05.052 --> 14:06.178
[growling]

14:06.262 --> 14:07.930
What's that horrible monster?!

14:08.013 --> 14:10.891
Go, Johnson! Take these guys out!

14:10.975 --> 14:13.769
- [snarling ferociously]
- [screaming maniacally]

14:13.853 --> 14:14.728
[grunts]

14:15.563 --> 14:16.981
Knives don't work on it!

14:18.315 --> 14:19.149
[grunts]

14:19.733 --> 14:22.611
- [Kasukabe] Let's escape while we can.
- [Thirteen] Grab a hold of me!

14:23.612 --> 14:25.281
[Kasukabe] Oh, the entrance is...

14:25.364 --> 14:27.366
Stupid insect, always doing too much!

14:27.449 --> 14:29.368
- [Kasukabe] This way!
- Ah, jeez!

14:30.578 --> 14:32.997
Nishinoya, go kill those bastards!

14:33.080 --> 14:34.540
[cackles] All right!

14:35.374 --> 14:37.251
- [manic screeching]
- [Johnson grunts]

14:39.670 --> 14:40.713
Hiratsuka!

14:42.423 --> 14:43.340
[gasps]

14:43.424 --> 14:45.801
[snarling ferociously]

14:48.554 --> 14:50.055
[dramatic music playing]

14:53.058 --> 14:55.519
- [gasping]
- What should we do, Kento?

14:56.770 --> 14:58.731
[Kento] I don't know if it will work, but...

14:58.814 --> 14:59.732
Take this!

14:59.815 --> 15:01.609
[Johnson chittering, shrieking]

15:02.234 --> 15:04.111
[floorboards creaking]

15:06.697 --> 15:08.616
Oh crap, those creeps are coming after us.

15:10.951 --> 15:12.703
[laughing evilly]

15:13.203 --> 15:15.039
- I... I'm so cold...
- You two wait here.

15:15.122 --> 15:16.415
I'll act as a decoy.

15:16.498 --> 15:17.583
P... Professor...

15:18.083 --> 15:19.668
[uneasy music playing]

15:20.586 --> 15:22.212
[laughs evilly]

15:22.713 --> 15:26.133
[both whimpering fearfully]

15:28.510 --> 15:29.637
- [Kasukabe] Hey!
- Huh?

15:29.720 --> 15:31.138
Over here!

15:31.221 --> 15:32.890
- [dramatic music playing]
- [cackles]

15:32.973 --> 15:34.141
[breathing heavily]

15:36.226 --> 15:38.145
- And it's a dead end. Huh?
- [clattering]

15:40.981 --> 15:42.775
[gasps] Huh?

15:44.276 --> 15:45.778
That's Haru and me...

15:47.571 --> 15:49.448
[cackling maniacally]

15:49.531 --> 15:51.158
I found you!

15:51.742 --> 15:56.789
Now I'm gonna cut you
into itty bitty pieces! [cackles]

15:56.872 --> 15:58.165
What did you do?

15:58.248 --> 16:01.794
Did you kill Haru
and steal this house from her?

16:01.877 --> 16:03.045
[shrieking]

16:05.005 --> 16:06.090
[gasping]

16:10.970 --> 16:13.013
[pained growling]

16:14.807 --> 16:16.141
[spray hissing]

16:17.476 --> 16:18.978
He's one tough bug.

16:19.061 --> 16:22.147
Oh yeah, he is, but not for much longer!

16:22.231 --> 16:24.400
I'll see you in hell, pest!

16:26.902 --> 16:27.987
Huh?

16:31.490 --> 16:32.366
[weak groaning]

16:32.449 --> 16:33.784
Listen, boys,

16:33.867 --> 16:37.705
didn't your mama ever teach you
that it's wrong to torture bugs?

16:37.788 --> 16:40.874
And this bug belongs
to my acquaintance's acquaintance!

16:40.958 --> 16:43.836
So if you're looking for a fight,
I'm right here. [gasps]

16:43.919 --> 16:46.797
- Go eat some sap or whatever it is you do!
- [chittering]

16:47.881 --> 16:51.510
Huh? And now that I'm looking,
you seem like Cross-Eyes to me.

16:51.593 --> 16:54.638
Guess my worrying saved me the trouble
of having to hunt you down.

16:54.722 --> 16:59.268
This is Noi, one of En's cousins.
A healing-type Sorcerer, I hear.

16:59.351 --> 17:01.145
A worthy prey indeed.

17:01.228 --> 17:04.732
[chuckling smugly] Well, come at me.
I'll beat the hell out of ya.

17:04.815 --> 17:07.651
[breathing raggedly]
Thank you for this, Boss.

17:11.697 --> 17:15.117
Well, whaddya know.
Looks like I ended up coming too.

17:15.200 --> 17:16.660
- [Johnson chittering]
- What?

17:16.744 --> 17:18.579
Little Bug? What's wrong with you?

17:18.662 --> 17:21.081
Shocking! Shocking! Shocking! Shocking!

17:24.168 --> 17:26.587
[man] This asshole was a woman?

17:27.171 --> 17:29.339
Amazingly done, Kento.

17:29.423 --> 17:32.092
To think you would one-hit KO Noi.

17:32.176 --> 17:35.220
[Kento] I just did
what the boss taught me to do.

17:35.304 --> 17:36.597
[chuckles delightedly]

17:36.680 --> 17:39.600
I'll dissect her. Rip off her clothes.

17:39.683 --> 17:41.101
[man chuckles] Got it.

17:43.395 --> 17:45.189
[ragged inhaling]

17:47.316 --> 17:49.985
[shin] Well, well,
you guys seem to be having fun.

17:50.569 --> 17:51.737
[Kento] Shin!

17:52.446 --> 17:53.322
Don't move!

17:54.656 --> 17:57.785
All I have to do
is slightly twist this knife,

17:57.868 --> 17:59.995
no more than if I were turning a tap,

18:00.079 --> 18:04.083
and the devil tumor inside her head
will become such a mess

18:04.166 --> 18:08.587
that not even Kikurage will be able
to resurrect her. [chuckling]

18:08.670 --> 18:10.589
[tense music playing]

18:15.761 --> 18:16.887
[chuckles]

18:16.970 --> 18:19.389
Well, aren't you a fast learner?

18:19.473 --> 18:22.601
Take this! And this! And this!

18:22.684 --> 18:23.602
[Shin splutters]

18:25.521 --> 18:27.106
[chuckling cruelly] And this!

18:28.357 --> 18:30.609
[Shin] Noi, if it were you...

18:30.692 --> 18:33.737
[Noi] Come on, Shin!
Stop worrying about me!

18:34.238 --> 18:38.367
I'd rather die than let myself
get beaten without a fight!

18:38.450 --> 18:40.953
[Shin] ...that's probably what you'd say.

18:41.453 --> 18:42.746
But you know what?

18:43.622 --> 18:44.873
I just...

18:52.464 --> 18:53.382
[body thuds]

19:07.563 --> 19:09.898
[heartbeat thumping]

19:12.234 --> 19:13.902
[heartbeat speeds up]

19:16.572 --> 19:18.657
[Shin] Yeah, that does it.

19:20.242 --> 19:23.620
If you wanted to piss me off,
you succeeded!

19:24.746 --> 19:26.039
[Kasukabe groans]

19:26.123 --> 19:27.666
Ouch, ouch, ouch.

19:27.749 --> 19:29.626
I can't believe I'm still alive.

19:29.710 --> 19:31.170
- [Nishinoya] Found you!
- Huh?

19:31.253 --> 19:33.630
[cackling]

19:33.714 --> 19:35.132
Prepare yourself!

19:35.215 --> 19:36.550
[shrieking]

19:36.633 --> 19:38.510
- [metal clanging]
-]groans]

19:38.594 --> 19:41.013
- [Shin] You okay, Kasukabe?
- [Kasukabe] Shin!

19:41.096 --> 19:44.516
- You came to save us!
- It's dangerous, so stand back.

19:44.600 --> 19:46.351
But, Shin, those injuries...

19:46.435 --> 19:47.936
[Shin grunts softly]

19:48.020 --> 19:50.314
My consciousness is fading away.

19:50.397 --> 19:53.275
My only option is to use Magic
and finish things quickly.

19:53.358 --> 19:56.195
- [Kasukabe] Oh, it ran away.
- [Shin] No, that's not it.

19:57.404 --> 20:00.407
The bastard knows
what kind of Magic I can do.

20:01.200 --> 20:06.371
Given that he's scared of that ability,
there's only one point he can attack.

20:06.455 --> 20:07.623
[shrieking]

20:07.706 --> 20:09.416
[Kasukabe gasps, wails]

20:11.835 --> 20:13.253
[cackling]

20:14.463 --> 20:16.757
Time to drop dead! [gasps]

20:17.382 --> 20:19.134
The smoke... where is it?

20:19.218 --> 20:20.510
[cackling]

20:20.594 --> 20:24.640
Maybe now you understand how it feels
to be someone who can't use Magic.

20:24.723 --> 20:26.934
[shrieking cackle]

20:27.017 --> 20:28.393
- Shin!
- Bastard...

20:28.477 --> 20:30.604
You can't fight when you're hurt this bad.

20:30.687 --> 20:31.772
[cackling]

20:31.855 --> 20:33.232
What, are you surprised?

20:33.315 --> 20:36.610
We practice how
to defeat Sorcerers every day, ha!

20:36.693 --> 20:39.112
- You practice this?
- Look, Shin.

20:39.196 --> 20:43.033
It's most likely that they stabbed you
directly in the Sorcerer's weak point.

20:43.116 --> 20:45.494
Weak point?
That's the first I ever heard of it!

20:45.577 --> 20:49.998
Sorcerers possess a very special organ
that is capable of producing smoke.

20:50.082 --> 20:54.127
If you've ever been stabbed there,
you won't be able to use any Magic!

20:54.211 --> 20:56.004
Now I understand.

20:56.088 --> 20:59.007
That must be how they beat Noi so easily.

20:59.508 --> 21:02.886
In fact, lately,
she hasn't even bothered dodging attacks.

21:02.970 --> 21:04.429
[Shin laughs]

21:05.055 --> 21:08.392
Ah, it's been a while
since things got this fun.

21:09.101 --> 21:10.269
[cackling]

21:10.352 --> 21:13.522
So you think it's "fun"
that you're about to be slaughtered?

21:13.605 --> 21:16.608
Yeah. Somehow reminds me of my childhood!

21:16.692 --> 21:18.568
[dramatic music playing]

21:18.652 --> 21:21.697
- [Nishinoya shrieking]
- [Shin grunting]

21:26.660 --> 21:27.661
[shrieks]

21:27.744 --> 21:29.121
[Shin grunts ferociously]

21:32.666 --> 21:34.960
- [grunts painfully]
- [cackling]

21:35.043 --> 21:39.589
Looks like you're "hammer"-strung!
Ha-ha-ha! I've got you now!

21:39.673 --> 21:42.134
- Prepare to die!
- [heaves]

21:42.676 --> 21:44.011
[shrieks]

21:47.306 --> 21:48.890
[Shin retching]

21:50.809 --> 21:52.728
[breathing heavily]

21:55.314 --> 21:58.233
Looks like I had another trick
up my sleeve after all!

21:58.317 --> 22:00.360
Ugh! [disgusted shrieking]

22:00.444 --> 22:01.737
[wailing]

22:01.820 --> 22:04.114
You're not getting away.

22:04.197 --> 22:06.450
[grunting fearfully]

22:07.534 --> 22:08.660
[screaming]

22:08.744 --> 22:10.579
- [Shin grunts]
- [shrieking]

22:14.207 --> 22:15.667
[Shin grunts loudly]

22:15.751 --> 22:19.546
Come on, just one more hit.
There's no need to hold back!

22:19.629 --> 22:20.714
No, wait--

22:20.797 --> 22:21.923
[music fades]

22:22.007 --> 22:24.217
[wet squelching]

22:28.472 --> 22:30.182
[Kasukabe] This is amazing.

22:30.265 --> 22:33.560
He went through
quite an unusual surgery here.

22:34.227 --> 22:37.814
I think it's an operation
to enable the use of Magic.

22:37.898 --> 22:40.275
[labored breathing] Time to get going.

22:40.359 --> 22:42.861
[grunts painfully]
Noi still needs my help.

22:42.944 --> 22:45.197
Huh? Those things captured Noi?

22:45.280 --> 22:46.740
But your injuries...

22:46.823 --> 22:50.160
It's honestly incredible
you're still alive after all that.

22:50.243 --> 22:52.329
That's because I train on a daily basis.

22:52.412 --> 22:53.705
More importantly for you,

22:54.331 --> 22:56.666
there's a big glass shard in your head.

22:56.750 --> 22:58.418
- Huh?
- Here, look.

22:58.919 --> 22:59.961
[Kasukabe grunts]

23:00.045 --> 23:01.088
Uh...

23:01.755 --> 23:03.757
[dreamy, tinkling music playing]

23:13.100 --> 23:14.643
[pleasant music playing]

23:17.229 --> 23:19.523
[adult Kasukabe] What are you doing
out here in the rain?

23:20.023 --> 23:21.608
Are you hurt somewhere?

23:24.194 --> 23:25.529
What's your name?

23:25.612 --> 23:28.657
There's no need to worry.
I'm a doctor, after all.

23:28.740 --> 23:30.117
Though a somewhat new one.

23:33.245 --> 23:35.372
My name is Kasukabe.

23:35.872 --> 23:39.126
But everyone else,
they all just call me Haru.

23:39.209 --> 23:42.337
[adult Kasukabe] Nice to meet you, Haru.
My name is...

23:42.421 --> 23:44.131
[Shin] Kasukabe!

23:44.214 --> 23:45.382
Kasukabe, hey!

23:46.675 --> 23:47.884
[Kasukabe groans]

23:47.968 --> 23:50.345
[gasps] Hey, are you doing all right?

23:50.429 --> 23:51.763
[Kasukabe] Y... yeah.

23:51.847 --> 23:52.931
[relieved sigh]

23:53.598 --> 23:54.766
[grunts]

23:56.560 --> 23:58.854
[Kasukabe] Haru, can it be true?

23:59.354 --> 24:01.481
Are you really... dead?

24:01.565 --> 24:02.899
[intriguing music playing]

24:03.692 --> 24:05.402
- Hey, Shin.
- Huh?

24:07.237 --> 24:09.739
Is there any chance
you could take me with you?

24:09.823 --> 24:12.659
Huh? Sure, if you want.

24:12.742 --> 24:15.287
As long as you don't slow me down, 'kay?

24:15.370 --> 24:17.414
My partner is in a tight spot here.

24:18.081 --> 24:19.166
[Kasukabe] I know.

24:20.417 --> 24:21.668
Well in any case,

24:21.751 --> 24:25.338
I can really see now how important
Noi has become for you, Shin.

24:25.922 --> 24:28.300
It seems like you've done some growing up.

24:28.383 --> 24:29.551
[Shin] Shut up!

24:29.634 --> 24:31.011
[music fades]

24:33.722 --> 24:35.724
[Japanese theme song playing]

26:01.685 --> 26:02.894
THE END

26:02.978 --> 26:05.063
[narrator] What we learned in Episode 13.

26:05.146 --> 26:07.274
The guys from the Cross-Eyes
are super frugal.

26:07.357 --> 26:09.401
The guys from the Hole are all smokers.

26:09.484 --> 26:11.194
Shin and Noi don't need women.

26:11.278 --> 26:15.615
What we're going to learn in Episode 14,
it's still... lost in chaos.

26:15.699 --> 26:17.909
This is... Dorohedoro!
